RULES:
- narration must equal all scene narration strings joined in scene order with one space;
- scene_id values must be sequential S1, S2, S3...;
- every scene must cite 1-4 valid evidence_ids from the supplied list;
- each scene must contain exactly 1 shot;
- each scene narration must be an exact contiguous segment of the continuous narration with 2-10 words; scene boundaries MAY occur inside a sentence because they are visual cut points, so a segment may start lowercase or end with comma/no terminal punctuation; the joined scene narrations must form natural complete narration that starts normally and ends with . ! ? or …;
- if a scene narration segment begins with a relative/anaphoric word such as which/that/it, który/która/które, который/которая/которое, який/яка/яке, first resolve what noun/result the pronoun actually refers to; do NOT assume it refers to the previous shot primary when the previous narration introduced another referent after that primary; if it does refer to the previous visual primary, keep that primary unless the current segment explicitly names a new concrete primary; never switch to an object unrelated to the actual referent/current clause;
- visual metadata must be grounded in the current narration segment plus the immediately preceding unfinished clause when the scene cut occurs inside one sentence;
- shot_id must start with its scene_id, for example S2-A or S2-B;
- each shot must have a concrete visual_intent, at least one must_show concept, and exactly 3 distinct English queries;
- CRITICAL LANGUAGE SPLIT: narration/scenes use OUTPUT LANGUAGE, but ALL visual metadata fields (visual_intent, every must_show item, every must_not_show item, and every queries_en item) MUST be written in English only regardless of OUTPUT LANGUAGE;
- never translate visual metadata into Polish, Russian, or Ukrainian; only spoken narration uses the requested non-English language;
- visual_intent must prefer a directly searchable real physical subject/result; for a specialized process, show the exact equipment if common, otherwise show the immediate physical input/output that proves the step;
- must_show must contain 1-3 SHORT independent English visual anchors, each 1-3 words; do not put a whole sentence/action phrase in one must_show item;
